In the early (mines and sokoban) and middle (castle and medusa)
games base damage by the weapon matters, but less and less as
your weapons get switched with artifacts and then enchanted up.  In
the late (VotD and below) there are so many silver hating monsters
that +d20 overwhelms the base damage of any other non-artifact
weapon.  A silver dagger ends up beating a dwarvish mattock for
damage but what folks actually enchant is a silver saber not a silver
dagger.  In the late game the silver hating monsters are the strongest
and most important to take out quickly.

The difference between artifacts and (good) non-artifacts is large
enough that the base damage of the secondary wield isn't as
important.  And the enchantment matters more than the base
damage - A +7 club beats any +0 non-artifact weapon no matter
the type except for silver weapons against silver haters.

So is it worth twohand wielding Snickersnee or Excalibur and your
original katana vs Snick/Excal and the first silver saber you enounter
in the game?  Eventually that silver saber will matter enough to be
worth a slot and the difference in the middle game isn't worth
keeping the non-artifact katana.  At least exercise the saber to
get the skill and use all ?oEW on it to the exclusion of the original
katan then switch when their enchantments match.


